*> Command feedback (docs/protocol/15-commands-framework.md §10.3, §10.4, §4.6): what the source and the operators are told.
*> The source is BR-SRC (core/copy/BRRUN.cpy); a text is a PB-TEXT translate component with literal arguments (09 §1).
*>
*> Entry points:
*>   BR-TELL USING player row (0 = the console), PB-TEXT: System Chat (overlay false) to the player, or a console line
*>   BR-TELL-STYLED USING player row, PB-TEXT, PB-TEXT-STYLE: the same with the style of the component (a console line is plain)
*>   BR-SYSTEM-CHAT-STYLED-BUILD USING PB-TEXT, PB-TEXT-STYLE, PB-BUFFER: System Chat 0x7C with a styled component
*>   BR-FEEDBACK USING PB-TEXT, broadcast flag (1 = B in the catalog): sendSuccess: silent sources send nothing; the source gets
*>     the text when it is the console or the game rule send_command_feedback is true; with the flag set and that rule true every
*>     other online operator gets chat.type.admin [source name, the text in English] gray and italic, and a source that is not
*>     the console is also logged to the console when log_admin_commands is true
*>   BR-FEEDBACK-STYLED USING PB-TEXT, PB-TEXT-STYLE, broadcast flag: the same with the style of the component for the source
*>   BR-FAILURE USING PB-TEXT: sendFailure: the text red to the source unless the source is silent
*>   BR-FAIL-EXCEPTION: the exception of BR-ERR (its key and arguments, no input context) red to the source (15 §10.4)
*>   BR-PARSE-ERROR USING player row: the two System Chat lines of a parse error (15 §4.6; BR-ERROR-TEXT) for BR-ERR and BR-IN

